          "lastChanged": "2026-10-02",
          "instrument": "Law No. 6/2017; Chief Executive Dispatch No. 227/2017"
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        "Macao Customs lets each passenger bring in, without declaring it, up to 19 cigarettes, 1 cigar (of no more than 3 g) and 25 g of leaf tobacco, and 1 litre of drinks over 30% alcohol; declare anything beyond these quantities.",
        "Canada's travel advice says it is prohibited to import, export or distribute e-cigarettes, vaporizers and their refills in Macao, and that offenders can expect heavy fines."
      ]
    }
